[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-01 (pending-fact-drives-topic-suppression): Does bullet 2's topic-suppression require the grounding fact to be counsellor-APPROVED (matching bullet 3's explicit qualifier and B3's approval gate), or does an unapproved, needs-review extraction suffice on its own? If a pending, later-rejected 'India-only' reading pre-emptively hides all visa content before the counsellor confirms it, an application draft could miss a needed visa step -- the contract does not say which way to fail safe here.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-02 (staleness-of-approved-facts): Does an approved fact stay permanently un-askable, or is there an implicit staleness window (tied to validFrom/validTo, session boundaries, or elapsed time) after which the counsellor may legitimately re-confirm it? The contract states no expiry condition or re-confirmation trigger.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-03 (do-not-ask-granularity): Is a do-not-ask entry always scoped to one exact fact key, always a broader topic/category, or does the counsellor/student choose the granularity per entry? Without a stated matching rule, an implementation could reasonably go either narrower or broader than intended on every entry.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-04 (do-not-ask-revocability): Can a student (or counsellor, on the student's behalf) revoke a do-not-ask entry mid-session or in a later session? If so, what confirms the revocation and where is it recorded? The contract is silent on the list's mutability entirely.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-05 (same-turn-race-ordering): When a destination-changing fact and an item's generation happen within the same turn or processing step, does suppression apply based on the fact state before or after that turn's update lands? The contract's outcome-only phrasing does not specify a snapshot boundary.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-06 (keyword-vs-semantic-topic-matching): Is a 'topic' for bullet-2 purposes matched via a fixed, contract- (or code-) defined category list (e.g. visa, financial-aid, exam-prep, ...), or via free-text/keyword similarity between the destination fact and the item's wording? A paraphrase that avoids the literal word 'visa' (e.g. 'entry permit') would be handled very differently under each reading, and the contract does not say which is intended.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-07 (partial-or-soft-intent-signal): Does an explicitly undecided, deferred-intent fact like this leave the visa topic simply un-suppressed (nothing has made it irrelevant yet), or does the contract intend some softer treatment (e.g. lower-priority evidence-only content, no direct questions) for genuinely uncertain destination signals? B18 has no concept of partial relevance, only a binary suppress/surface outcome.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-08 (cross-session-persistence-of-known): Does bullet 3's 'never asked again' apply across the student's entire longitudinal history (any prior session), or is 'already known' scoped to the current session only? If longitudinal, does staleness (b18-u-02) or a counsellor override ever reopen it?
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-09 (comparison-card-reopening-decided-choice): Does bullet 3's protection against re-asking extend to a comparison card that implicitly invites reconsidering an already-approved, already-decided choice, or does it apply only to the literal question-type re-ask (as F9-03's non-reopening comparison example assumes)? The contract does not distinguish 'informative comparison using a known value' from 'comparison that invites revisiting a settled decision'.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-10 (third-party-voiced-facts-and-do-not-ask): Does a do-not-ask instruction or a fact voiced by a parent/guardian in a joint counselling session carry the same weight under B18 as one voiced by the student directly? The contract's 'student's own facts' / 'student's do-not-ask list' wording does not address multi-speaker sessions at all.
[t039][quarantined, not asserted] b18-u-11 (retracting-already-surfaced-items): When a fact that justified showing an item later changes (e.g. a withdrawn application), must an already-displayed card/item be retracted or hidden, or does B18 only govern what gets produced going forward? The contract's outcome language is about production, not retroactive retraction of prior output.
